// The light a model takes from the frame, given where the model stands.
// `interior` is rgb = the MOHD ambient of the WMO whose interior group holds
// the model, w = 1 when an interior group holds it and 0 outdoors.
//
// The sun does not reach an interior group. wmo.frag lights one from MOHD and
// its baked vertex colours and ignores the frame's light, so a model inside
// takes the same ambient and no directional light, and matches the walls
// around it. The frame's own light stays the outdoor one, which is what lights
// everything seen through a door.
//
// An all-zero ambient is not taken: with no directional light beside it the
// model would draw black, so the frame's ambient is kept.
vec3 interiorAmbient(vec4 interior, vec3 frameAmbient) {
    bool usable = interior.w > 0.5f && interior.r + interior.g + interior.b > 0.0f;
    return usable ? vec3(interior.r, interior.g, interior.b) : frameAmbient;
}

// The share of the frame's directional light a model takes.
float interiorSunScale(vec4 interior) {
    return interior.w > 0.5f ? 0.0f : 1.0f;
}
